        // structure, the flat cadence domain, and why rungs 2 and 3 are Missing-with-measurements.
        //
        // RealVisXL is the only entry in the family with a rung-4 row on ALL THREE tiers, measured
        // at 1024²/4 steps against its own staged control: bf16 19.003 → 14.936 GiB (−21.40%),
        // q8 17.693 → 15.516 (−12.31%), q4 16.654 → 15.493 (−6.97%), byte-identical output.
        // Its bf16 resident baseline is 20.513 GiB and rung 1 alone takes that to 19.003 (−7.4%).
        //
        // The bf16 tier publishes overlay `none` only: `adapters_are_replayable` refuses a LoRA load
