        //     that tier's snapshot cannot arm the window. The cause is the SNAPSHOT, not the
        //     architecture: `unet/` IS genuinely packed (u32 codes with .scales/.biases, 3.46 GiB,
        //     byte-for-byte realvisxl q8's shape, and its measured 17.693 GiB staged peak is
        //     realvisxl q8's to the millibyte) but `unet/config.json` ships WITHOUT the
        //     `quantization` marker. `mlx_gen::quant::packed_quant_bits` reads that marker and only
        //     that marker, so `needs_load_time_quant` returns true, `load_leaves_blocks_lazy` is
        //     false and `streamable` refuses. The rung fails closed, which is correct -- a window
        //     over an already-materialized trunk bounds nothing. The repair is a republished
        //     snapshot rather than a looser predicate; tracked as inference sc-17522. (The same
        //     missing marker also makes `warn_sequential_requantize` fire on every load of these
        //     two.)
      },
