        // tier's config.json so nothing quantizes at load). The worker resolves env override
        // (SCENEWORKS_MLX_WAN5B_DIR) → local <data>/models/mlx/wan_2_2 (a local conversion supersedes)
        // → the requested tier subdir of this snapshot (wan_tier_subdir), loading with no install-time
        // convert peak. Source Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B is Apache-2.0; converter "wan_ti2v_5b" builds the
        // bf16 tier and the q8/q4 tiers are derived from it (quantize_wan_transformer, group 64).
        "minMemoryGb": 45,
        "repo": "SceneWorks/wan2.2-ti2v-5b-mlx",
        // macOS curated menu (sc-7296): mlx Wan adopts the unified framework over its native
        // flow σ schedule, adding `dpmpp_2m` (native FLOW-SNR DPM++2M) on top of the base set.
        // No scheduler axis (the flow shift is `scheduler_shift`).
        "limits": {
          "samplers": ["default", "uni_pc", "euler", "dpmpp_2m", "euler_ancestral", "heun", "dpmpp_sde", "ddim"],
          "schedulers": ["default"]
        }
      },
      // candle/CUDA VRAM gate — RE-DROPPED onto the sequential-offload path (sc-13175), which SUPERSEDES
      // the RESIDENT numbers sc-12631 shipped (q4 46.1 / q8 48.7 / bf16 54.0, minMemoryGb 48). The engine
      // already wired dense component offload for the 5B (sc-12757: flush the UMT5 TE + z48 VAE off-GPU
      // around the denoise), so `video_jobs::candle_wan_offload_policy` now forces `OffloadPolicy::Sequential`
      // for `wan2_2_ti2v_5b` and these are that SEQUENTIAL peak — the residency the load actually takes.
      //
      // MEASURED on an idle RTX PRO 6000 (Blackwell sm_120) via the candle-gen-wan VramProbe harness
      // (candle-gen-wan/tests/vram_probe.rs) at this model's OWN shipped default — 832x480, 121 frames
      // (5s @ 24fps), 20 steps, CFG on — with `CANDLE_GEN_OFFLOAD=sequential`. Each tier in its own process
      // (cudarc's caching allocator never returns pages, so a second tier in-process re-reports the first's
      // high-water). Renders coherent (middle-frame std 75–78, matching the sc-12757 parity datum 75.6).
      //
      // THE PEAK IS THE DENOISE, NOT THE DECODE, and it is now DiT-only resident: sequential offload holds
      // just the DiT + the tier-blind chunked-sdpa attention transient during denoise (the bf16 UMT5 TE,
      // sc-12778, is dropped before it; the z48 VAE is loaded only for decode). The z48 vae22 decode is the
      // LOWER phase (8.32 GiB, tier-blind), so the reported ceiling is card-independent. q4 and q8, each
      // measured in its OWN process, land on the SAME 12.1 GB pool high-water: the peak is the attention
      // transient, not the weights, so their DiT code-size delta shows up only in STEADY residency
      // (pre-decode nvidia-smi 4.9 → 7.1 GB) and never reaches the pool-block-quantized watermark. Only the
      // dense bf16 DiT lifts it (14.5 GB).
      //
      // vramGbByTier here is the nvidia-smi POOL high-water (base-10 GB) — the real max device footprint,
      // since cudarc never frees the pool back to the driver — NOT the lower driver-mempool USED_MEM_HIGH
      // (`CU_MEMPOOL_ATTR_USED_MEM_HIGH`, sc-12818: 10.61 / 10.61 / 11.67 GiB concurrent-live). Gating at the
      // POOL high-water is the disciplined answer to the sc-13174 pool-vs-USED_MEM_HIGH caveat: it needs NO
      // assumption that the pool packs down under memory pressure on a small card (the assumption that made
      // the A14B defer q8/bf16 as `measured: false`), so all three 5B tiers ship honestly `measured: true`.
      // It is still far under the target — q4/q8 admit a 16 GB card (12.1 + 2 = 14.1) and bf16 a 24 GB one
      // (14.5 + 2 = 16.5), where the resident gate needed ~48. (The decode's free-aware `WAN_VAE_BUDGET_GIB`
      // was pinned during measurement because its auto path reads MIN free across ALL GPUs and a co-tenant
      // GPU poisons it; the decode is not the peak, so the budget only moves decode tiling, never this ceiling.)
      //
      // minMemoryGb 14 gates the DEFAULT/lightest (q4) tier (12.1 + the gate's 2 GB headroom); the per-tier
      // `wan_video_fit_error` (`vramGbByTier + 2`) is the real admission decision, so bf16 is still refused
      // below ~16.5 GB. The resolver prefers q8 when installed (sc-10726); q4 and q8 are identical, so
      // gating either is the same read. This model loads SEQUENTIAL, not resident — the gate is only truthful
      // because the load is coupled to it (pinned by the
      // `wan_candle_blocks_drive_the_video_fit_gate_and_reject` and
      // `candle_wan_sequential_engines_offload_others_resident` tripwires).
      "candle": {
        "minMemoryGb": 14,
        "vramGbByTier": { "q4": 12.1, "q8": 12.1, "bf16": 14.5 },
        "vramMeasuredPixels": 1048576,
        "measured": true
      },
