    // Krea Realtime 14B (epic 8431, sc-8444 S11): krea/krea-realtime-video, Apache-2.0 — the
    // Wan 2.1 T2V 14B backbone distilled via Self-Forcing into an AUTOREGRESSIVE generator. It
    // renders frame-blocks left-to-right against a rolling causal KV cache at ~6 few-step
    // denoises per block instead of one whole-clip diffusion, which is why it is its own engine
    // (mlx-gen-krea-realtime) rather than a Wan variant. macOS-only native MLX; there is no
    // candle path (the worker fails a non-mac job loudly, `video_jobs/mod.rs`).
    //
    // Distinct from the existing `krea_*` IMAGE lane (Krea 2 Turbo / Raw, engine `mlx-gen-krea`).
    // Same vendor, unrelated architecture — do not merge their ids, families, or LoRA families.
    {
      "id": "krea_realtime_14b",
      "name": "Krea Realtime 14B",
      "family": "krea-realtime",
      "type": "video",
      "adapter": "krea_realtime",
      // The engine routes purely on the conditioning the worker hands it (`pipeline::run`):
      // nothing → t2v, a Reference still → i2v (VAE-encoded to warm the AR KV cache), a
      // VideoClip source → v2v (a strength-controlled AR init). Those are exactly the three
      // capabilities declared here; the descriptor advertises no first/last-frame, clip-extend,
      // bridge, or person-replace surface, so none is claimed.
      "capabilities": [
        "text_to_video",
        "image_to_video",
        "video_to_video"
      ],
      // Which generation AXES this engine actually has (sc-8445), the video-lane sibling of the
      // `audio` sub-block. Krea Realtime is CFG-FREE: the Self-Forcing distillation baked guidance
      // out, so `generate_krea_realtime` runs a single batch-1 forward, sets `negative_prompt: None`
      // and never forwards a guidance scale (video_jobs/krea_realtime.rs). Declaring that here lets
      // Video Studio HIDE both controls instead of offering knobs the worker discards — and makes
      // this entry's own `ui.description` ("CFG-off, so there is no negative prompt or guidance
      // control") a true statement about the shipped UI rather than an aspiration.
      //
      // ⚠️ Polarity is the OPPOSITE of the `audio` block's: an ABSENT key here means TRUE. Of the
      // ten video entries, EIGHT genuinely take both (the Wan family, both LTX entries, SCAIL-2 and
      // Bernini) and declare nothing; the two that do not — this entry and `svd`, whose engine
      // drives its own frame-wise CFG ramp — declare it false right here. So absent-means-supported
      // is the correct default for the majority AND leaves those eight behaving exactly as they did
      // before this block existed. The schema says the same thing.
      "video": {
        "supportsGuidance": false,
        "supportsNegativePrompt": false
      },
      "downloads": [
        // macOS quant matrix (epic 8506 shape, mirroring scail2_14b): each tier is a SEPARATE
        // user-selectable artifact tagged with a `variant`; `q4` (default) installs when no tier
        // is chosen. Every tier subdir is fully self-contained — the Krea DiT at that tier's
        // precision plus the STOCK Wan 2.1 companions the engine reuses verbatim (z16 VAE, UMT5
        // text encoder, tokenizer) and a `config.json` carrying the AR fields — so the dense
        // companions repeat per tier and a tier dir is a complete `from_snapshot` tree.
        // Companions are byte-identical across all three tiers: t5_encoder 11,361,845,504 ·
        // vae 507,591,212 · tokenizer 16,837,417. Sizes below are the exact hosted byte counts
        // read back from the published repo tree, so `estimatedSizeBytes` is not an estimate.
        //
        // ⚠️ `files` are EXPLICIT PATHS, deliberately not a `<tier>/*` glob. The worker's glob
        // (`imports.rs::pattern_matches`, Rust `glob` with default MatchOptions) lets `*` cross
        // `/`, so `bf16/*` WOULD reach the nested `bf16/transformer/` shards — the download
        // itself is not the exposure. The exposure is CACHE HEALTH: `snapshot_contains_pattern`
        // (apps/rust-api/src/models.rs) treats a glob as satisfied by ANY one matching file, and
        // this repo ships no `model_index.json`, so the diffusers per-component augmentation is
        // a no-op for it — a tier that lost 6 of its 7 DiT shards would still read `installed`
        // and then die at load. Explicit paths make every file its own presence check (exact
        // `path_is_readable_file`) and its own download-time claim (sc-12283's per-pattern
        // hard-fail), so a torn tier reports `incomplete` and names the missing shard.
        {
          "provider": "huggingface",
          "repo": "SceneWorks/krea-realtime-14b-mlx",
          "revision": "e68e9a3d98187fdf6936838ffcf6df5aa48d6626",
          "variant": "q4",
          "default": true,
          "files": [
            "q4/config.json",
            "q4/dit.safetensors",
            "q4/t5_encoder.safetensors",
            "q4/tokenizer.json",
            "q4/vae.safetensors"
          ],
          "platforms": ["macos"],
          // Q4 DiT 8,378,982,809 + the shared dense companions. The default tier for this dense
